# Build context for `web/Dockerfile` (`docs/13-deployment-fly.md` §3).
#
# An allowlist: everything is excluded, then the sources the build needs are
# added back. A new top-level file therefore stays out of the image until
# someone lists it, which is the way round that fails safe for `.env`.

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.base.json
!litestream.yml
!packages
!scripts

# …minus what `packages/**` would otherwise drag in. `dist` is rebuilt inside
# the image; a host build would otherwise shadow it.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.data
**/*.tsbuildinfo
docs
.data
.env
.env.*
